  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% permanent test limit and the 8-per-100k model-level recall trigger, but S2 lets a model above 5% keep selling through an unspecified 'time-limited' remediation period, so the sales stop is not mandatory. Shut-off retrofit is set at six years and suppression at 36 months, both within acceptable ranges and aligned with the two sides' red lines. The S2 remediation length is not stated, so transition_months is recorded as open-ended (999)."
